{
  "an3.88:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 3.88 ",
  "an3.88:0.2": "9. Ascetics ",
  "an3.88:0.3": "Training (3rd) ",
  "an3.88:1.1": "“Mendicants, each fortnight over a hundred and fifty training rules come up for recitation, in which gentlemen who desire self-knowledge train. ",
  "an3.88:1.2": "These are all included in the three trainings. ",
  "an3.88:1.3": "What three? ",
  "an3.88:1.4": "The training in the higher ethics, the higher mind, and the higher wisdom. ",
  "an3.88:1.5": "These are the three trainings that include them all. ",
  "an3.88:2.1": "Take the case of a mendicant who has fulfilled their ethics, immersion, and wisdom. ",
  "an3.88:2.2": "They break some lesser and minor training rules, but are restored. ",
  "an3.88:2.3": "Why is that? ",
  "an3.88:2.4": "Because I don’t say they’re incapable of that. ",
  "an3.88:2.5": "But they’re constant and steady in their precepts regarding the training rules that are fundamental, befitting the spiritual path. They keep the rules they’ve undertaken. ",
  "an3.88:2.6": "They realize the undefiled freedom of heart and freedom by wisdom. And they live having realized it with their own insight in this very life due to the ending of defilements. ",
  "an3.88:2.7": "If they don’t penetrate so far, with the ending of the five lower fetters they’re extinguished between one life and the next. ",
  "an3.88:2.8": "If they don’t penetrate so far, with the ending of the five lower fetters they’re extinguished upon landing. ",
  "an3.88:2.9": "If t